kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[2]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,"error-envelope-actually-emitted-by-routes","Server routes MUST emit the ErrorEnvelope shape not ad-hoc error objects","All non-SSE error responses MUST return the ErrorEnvelope shape defined in packages/shared (error_code plus message plus optional details plus optional retry_after). MUST NOT return ad-hoc shapes such as {error: string} or {error plus error_code} or {error plus max_bytes plus uploaded_bytes}. Current feature routers return at least 5 ad-hoc shapes using field name error instead of canonical message, violating existing r3.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,"shared-error-envelope-helper","Server MUST provide a shared error-response helper consuming ErrorEnvelopeSchema","The system MUST provide a shared helper (sendError or setError) that consumes the ErrorEnvelopeSchema from packages/shared and centralizes the HTTP status to error_code mapping (400 maps to INVALID_REQUEST plus 404 maps to NOT_FOUND plus 409 maps to CONFLICT plus 422 maps to SCHEMA_VALIDATION_FAILED plus 429 maps to RATE_LIMITED plus 503 maps to MODEL_ERROR). Feature routers MUST return errors via this helper rather than constructing ad-hoc error bodies inline.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[3]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  "error-envelope-actually-emitted-by-routes","non-sse-error-shape",a feature router such as POST /v2/outputs hits a predictable error (source_id out of scope or SLIDES guard or schema validation failure),the system returns an error response,"the body MUST match ErrorEnvelopeSchema (with error_code and message) and MUST NOT be {error: string} or any other ad-hoc shape"
  "error-envelope-actually-emitted-by-routes","field-name-is-message",the client triggers a 400 error such as a missing field,the system returns an error response,the message field MUST be named message (aligned with ErrorEnvelopeSchema) and MUST NOT be named error
  "shared-error-envelope-helper","single-helper-source",a developer adds a new error branch in a feature router,returning the error via the shared helper,the helper output MUST be consistent with other routers and error_code MUST come from the centralized mapping table not a custom string
